  "notes": "{気|き}に{入|い}る is a common expression meaning to like or be pleased with something.\n\nCOMPONENTS:\n- {気|き}: feeling, spirit\n- に: into\n- {入|い}る: to enter\nLiterally: \"enters one's feeling\" = pleases\n\nFORMS:\n- {気|き}に{入|い}る: to like (plain)\n- {気|き}に{入|い}った: liked (past)\n- {気|き}に{入|い}らない: to not like\n- お{気|き}に{入|い}り: favorite (noun form)\n\nGRAMMAR:\n- What is liked takes が: この{服|ふく}が{気|き}に{入|い}った\n- Person who likes can be marked with は or は topic\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- お{気|き}に{入|い}りの〜: favorite ~\n- {気|き}に{入|い}ってもらえると{嬉|うれ}しい: I'd be happy if you like it",
